    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d782">

                <pb facs="0638" n="522" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg522"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/23455.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Special Commissioners to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Niagara Falls</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 2, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>We have just returned from a conference where we expressed the hope that the
                    Mediators would as soon as possible reply to the Zubáran communication. The
                    Mediators stated they had already drafted such a letter and read it to
                        us.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d782-f1"/> We found it to be couched in the most
                    courteous terms, stating substantially that they wrote to inquire whether they
                    were to understand that the Chief of the Constitutionalist Army desired to have
                    a representative in the conference on the terms stated in the original
                    correspondence and asking that if such was his intention he appoint delegates as
                    soon as possible.</p>
                <p>The Mediators then inquired if we were willing to continue the discussion of the
                    plan written by the Mediators. We assented and it was finally agreed that we
                    should put their plan in one column and in another parallel column our
                    modifications, suggestions or substitutes, as a working basis for future
                    discussions. This will require us to present something concrete and we should be
                    glad for you to have the double column prepared.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Commissioners</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d782-f1" n="32" xml:id="d782-f1-content">
                <p>The letter as sent is inclosed with Mr. Dodge’s No. 16 of June 13, post.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
